  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "Use the H(4,3) coordinate order (004,013,022,031,040,103,112,121,130,202,211,220,301,310,400). For every gamma in BR_{\\mathring Q}(4,3) intersect Z^{H(4,3)} satisfying gamma_103 <= 0, gamma_112 <= 0, gamma_301 <= 0, and gamma_alpha >= 0 at each of the other twelve coordinates, there exists C(gamma)>0 such that C(gamma)D_gamma-N_gamma is coefficientwise nonnegative in the twelve formal variables a_ri. This claim includes all boundary lattice points of that closed sign chamber and makes no assertion about integral cone points outside it; in particular it does not resolve the frozen universal conjecture.",
